# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# The context is the whole repository, and everything in it is sent to the
# daemon before the first instruction runs. `node_modules` alone is
# hundreds of megabytes that the image then discards and reinstalls, so
# excluding it is most of the build time. It would also be *wrong* to
# copy: a tree installed on Windows carries platform-specific binaries that
# do not run on Alpine.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Regenerated inside the image; copying a local `dist` risks
# shipping something compiled from uncommitted source.
dist
.next
.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. `.env` is gitignored and would still be picked up here, which is
# how credentials end up baked into an image layer and stay there even
# after a later instruction deletes the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# History and tooling — large, and none of it affects the build.
.git
.github
.husky
coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# Documentation and editor state.
docs
*.md
!README.md
.vscode
.idea
